<title>UK: Railtrack says trading &quot;in line&quot;.</title>
<headline>Railtrack says trading &quot;in line&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>British rail infrastructure group Railtrack Plc said on Wednesday that its trading performance in the current year to March 1997 &quot;is broadly in line with our objectives and expectations.&quot;</p>
<p>Chairman Robert Horton told Railtrack's annual general meeting that its recent privatisation &quot;was never going to be an easy ride.&quot; He said efforts to change the commercial culture of the organisation are now underway.</p>
<p>Horton said preliminary work has also begun on transforming some of its 14 major stations, including making full use of space, which will represent &quot;a major investment programme.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
